---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import Particles from '@components/Particles/Particles.vue';
import siteData from '@config/siteData.json';

const email = siteData.author.email;
const updated = '15 September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title={`${siteData.author.name} - Privacy`}
  description={`How ${siteData.author.name}'s website handles your data: hosting logs, the newsletter, email contact, and no cookies or analytics.`}
>
  <Particles client:only="vue" />
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-24 md:pt-36 lg:pt-44">
    <header>
      <h1 class="h1 text-pretty text-gradient lg:pb-2">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="description mt-6 text-pretty">
        This site collects as little as it can. Here is what is processed, by whom, and what you
        can do about it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="prose mt-14">
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {siteData.author.name}, the author of this site. For anything related to your data,
        write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static and served by Netlify, Inc. (United States). Like any web server,
        Netlify records access logs when you load a page: your IP address, browser identifier,
        the page requested and the time. Those logs exist to deliver the site and to protect it
        from abuse, on the basis of legitimate interest. Netlify keeps them for a limited time and
        commits to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses in its data processing agreement. See
        <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
          >Netlify's privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe, your email address is stored by Buttondown (Buttondown, LLC, United
        States), the service that sends the emails on my behalf. It is used for one thing: telling
        you when I publish something new. There is no fixed schedule.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The subscription is based on your consent, confirmed by the link in the first email
          (double opt-in). Nothing is sent until you confirm.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your address is kept until you unsubscribe. Every email has an unsubscribe link, and
          you can also write to me to be removed.
        </li>
        <li>
          The subscription page runs on Buttondown's servers, even though it lives under this
          domain. Buttondown may set its own cookies there and records basic delivery data for
          the emails it sends. See
          <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
            >Buttondown's privacy policy</a
          >.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to me, your message and address stay in my mailbox for as long as the
        conversation needs them. They are not shared with anyone or used for anything else.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        None. The site sets no cookies, stores nothing in your browser and runs no analytics.
        Fonts and scripts are served from this domain, so loading a page contacts no third party.
        The only external requests happen when you follow a link to another site, such as GitHub,
        LinkedIn, Kaggle or the newsletter page, each of which has its own policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you can ask to access, correct, delete or export the data held about you,
        object to or restrict its processing, and withdraw consent at any time. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and I will answer. You can also lodge a complaint
        with the Spanish data protection authority, the
        <a href="https://www.aepd.es/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">AEPD</a>, or with
        the authority in your own country.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If the way the site handles data changes, this page will change with it. Last updated on
        {updated}.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
